gartner-hypecycle-graph: 1
# A hand-authored hype cycle of energy breakthroughs, fusion's many variants among them, from the
# 1950s to ideas that have not started yet. Dates after 2026 are projections, and dates and
# influences are illustrative, not a claim: see readme.md.
trends:
  - id: stellarator
    name: Stellarator
    start: 1951-05
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 0
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 1961-01
    trough-end: 2015-12
    tags: [fusion, science]
    description: Lyman Spitzer's twisted magnetic bottle, eclipsed by the tokamak and revived by Wendelstein 7-X.
  - id: tokamak
    name: Tokamak
    start: 1968-08
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 2
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 1985-11
    trough-end: 2021-12
    tags: [fusion, science]
    description: The Soviet T-3 results of 1968 made the tokamak the mainstream of magnetic fusion; ITER is its largest descendant.
  - id: inertial-confinement-fusion
    name: Inertial confinement fusion
    start: 1972-09
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 4
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 1985-01
    trough-end: 2022-12
    tags: [fusion, science]
    description: Lasers crush a fuel pellet; the National Ignition Facility passed ignition in December 2022.
  - id: high-temperature-superconductors
    name: High-temperature superconductors
    start: 1987-01
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 6
    phases: 4
    tags: [fusion, materials]
    description: Discovered in 1986; rare-earth barium copper oxide tape later made far stronger magnets possible.
  - id: cold-fusion
    name: Cold fusion
    start: 1989-03
    stop: 1998-01
    row: 8
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 1989-11
    tags: [fusion, science]
    description: Fleischmann and Pons's tabletop claim, which no one could reproduce.
  - id: field-reversed-configuration
    name: Field-reversed configuration
    start: 1998-04
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 8
    phases: 2
    tags: [fusion]
    description: TAE Technologies' route, aimed in the long run at aneutronic proton-boron fuel.
  - id: magnetized-target-fusion
    name: Magnetized target fusion
    start: 2002-01
    stop: 2038-01
    row: 10
    phases: 2
    tags: [fusion]
    description: General Fusion squeezes a magnetised plasma inside a liquid-metal wall driven by pistons.
  - id: pulsed-magneto-inertial-fusion
    name: Pulsed magneto-inertial fusion
    start: 2013-01
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 12
    phases: 1
    tags: [fusion]
    description: Helion fires two plasmoids into each other and recovers the electricity directly.
  - id: sheared-flow-z-pinch
    name: Sheared-flow Z-pinch
    start: 2017-01
    stop: 2038-01
    row: 14
    phases: 1
    tags: [fusion]
    description: Zap Energy's pinch, kept stable by flowing plasma instead of magnets.
  - id: compact-high-field-tokamak
    name: Compact high-field tokamak
    start: 2018-03
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 16
    phases: 1
    tags: [fusion]
    description: Commonwealth Fusion Systems' SPARC, a tokamak shrunk by stronger magnets.
  - id: fusion-power-plants
    name: Fusion power plants
    start: 2029-01
    stop: 2055-01
    row: 18
    phases: 1
    tags: [fusion, upcoming]
    description: The first plants to put fusion electricity on a grid, as ARC and Helion's Orion plan to.
  - id: lunar-helium-3
    name: Lunar helium-3
    start: 2031-01
    stop: 2055-01
    row: 6
    phases: 1
    tags: [fusion, space, conceptual]
    description: Mining the Moon's regolith for helium-3, a fuel for aneutronic fusion.
  - id: fission-power
    name: Nuclear fission power
    start: 1954-06
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 20
    phases: 4
    peak-end: 1979-03
    trough-end: 2000-01
    slope-end: 2011-03
    tags: [nuclear]
    description: From Obninsk in 1954; halted by Three Mile Island and Chernobyl, and dependable ever since.
  - id: molten-salt-reactors
    name: Molten salt reactors
    start: 1965-06
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 22
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 1969-12
    trough-end: 2011-01
    tags: [nuclear]
    description: Oak Ridge's reactor experiment of the 1960s, revived by thorium advocates and new start-ups.
  - id: small-modular-reactors
    name: Small modular reactors
    start: 2007-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 24
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2023-11
    tags: [nuclear]
    description: Factory-built reactors; the first US project was cancelled in November 2023.
  - id: microreactors
    name: Microreactors
    start: 2018-03
    stop: 2038-01
    row: 26
    phases: 1
    tags: [nuclear]
    description: Reactors small enough for a truck, after NASA's KRUSTY test of 2018.
  - id: solar-photovoltaics
    name: Solar photovoltaics
    start: 1954-04
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 28
    phases: 4
    peak-end: 1980-01
    trough-end: 2000-01
    slope-end: 2012-01
    tags: [solar]
    description: From Bell Labs' silicon cell to the cheapest electricity ever built.
  - id: wind-power
    name: Wind power
    start: 1980-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 30
    phases: 4
    tags: [wind]
  - id: offshore-wind
    name: Offshore wind
    start: 1991-09
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 32
    phases: 3
    tags: [wind]
  - id: perovskite-solar-cells
    name: Perovskite solar cells
    start: 2012-10
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 34
    phases: 2
    tags: [solar, materials]
  - id: next-generation-geothermal
    name: Next-generation geothermal
    start: 2020-06
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 36
    phases: 1
    tags: [geothermal]
    description: Enhanced geothermal systems drilled with the oil and gas industry's techniques.
  - id: space-based-solar-power
    name: Space-based solar power
    start: 2023-06
    stop: 2050-01
    row: 38
    phases: 1
    tags: [solar, space, conceptual]
    description: Peter Glaser's idea of 1968, first beamed down from orbit by Caltech's MAPLE experiment in 2023.
  - id: superhot-rock-geothermal
    name: Superhot rock geothermal
    start: 2028-01
    stop: 2050-01
    row: 28
    phases: 1
    tags: [geothermal, conceptual]
    description: Millimetre-wave drilling down to rock hot enough to make water supercritical.
  - id: lithium-ion-batteries
    name: Lithium-ion batteries
    start: 1991-06
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 40
    phases: 4
    tags: [storage]
  - id: hydrogen-fuel-cells
    name: Hydrogen fuel cells
    start: 1998-01
    stop: 2012-01
    row: 42
    phases: 2
    tags: [hydrogen]
    description: The hydrogen economy of the early 2000s, which cars never followed.
  - id: electric-vehicles
    name: Electric vehicles
    start: 2008-02
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 44
    phases: 3
    tags: [transport, storage]
  - id: solid-state-batteries
    name: Solid-state batteries
    start: 2017-01
    stop: 2034-01
    row: 42
    phases: 2
    tags: [storage, materials]
  - id: grid-scale-batteries
    name: Grid-scale batteries
    start: 2017-12
    stop: 2036-01
    row: 46
    phases: 2
    tags: [storage, grid]
  - id: green-hydrogen
    name: Green hydrogen
    start: 2019-06
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 48
    phases: 2
    tags: [hydrogen]
  - id: room-temperature-superconductors
    name: Room-temperature superconductors
    start: 2023-07
    stop: 2025-07
    row: 50
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2024-01
    tags: [materials, conceptual]
    description: LK-99's claim of July 2023, refuted within weeks; the breakthrough would change every grid and magnet.
  - id: smart-grid
    name: Smart grid
    start: 2007-12
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 52
    phases: 3
    tags: [grid]
  - id: ai-for-fusion-and-grids
    name: AI for fusion and grids
    start: 2022-02
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 54
    phases: 1
    tags: [grid, fusion, ai]
    description: Reinforcement learning shaped a tokamak's plasma in 2022; the same methods balance grids.
  - id: ai-data-centre-demand
    name: AI data-centre demand
    start: 2023-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 56
    phases: 1
    tags: [grid, ai]
    description: The load that sent AI companies to sign for nuclear, geothermal and fusion power.
